<!--
  ===========================================================================
  APIM policy  |  Azure AI Foundry  |  BASIC profile  |  GET /v1/models
  ===========================================================================
  Companion to wizard-foundry-policy-basic.xml. Apply it at OPERATION scope
  on a GET /v1/models operation, on the SAME API (URL suffix "openai") that
  already serves the chat traffic.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY YOU NEED IT
  ===========================================================================
  OpenAI compatible clients probe <base>/models to validate the connection
  and populate the model picker BEFORE they ever send a chat request. If that
  operation does not exist, APIM answers 404 and the client blames the model:

      Model 'gpt-5.1' not found on provider at
      https://<gateway-host>/openai/v1 (HTTP 404)

  That reads like a missing deployment, but it is a routing problem. The chat
  deployment is fine; DISCOVERY is what 404s. GitHub Copilot CLI and JetBrains
  AI Assistant both probe it. VS Code Custom Endpoint does not, which is why
  VS Code can work against a gateway where the CLI fails.

  ===========================================================================
  IT MUST BE THE SAME API, NOT A NEW ONE
  ===========================================================================
  The client builds the models URL from the one base URL you hand it, so an
  API published on any other suffix can never be reached. Add the operation
  to the API the chat traffic already uses.

  ===========================================================================
  APPLY AT OPERATION SCOPE, NOT API SCOPE
  ===========================================================================
  There is deliberately no <base /> in inbound or outbound here. The API level
  policy parses the request body, and a GET carries none, so inheriting it
  would break this call. Keep <base /> in backend and on-error.

  ===========================================================================
  BEFORE YOU APPLY IT
  ===========================================================================
  1. Replace REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FOUNDRY-BACKEND-ID with the same backend id
     you used in wizard-foundry-policy-basic.xml.
  2. Authentication to Foundry must MATCH wizard-foundry-policy-basic.xml.
     Both now ship with a managed-identity block. Replace
     REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FOUNDRY-MI-AUDIENCE with
         https://cognitiveservices.azure.com   (Azure Commercial)
         https://cognitiveservices.azure.us    (Azure Government)
     and grant the APIM managed identity "Cognitive Services OpenAI User" on
     the Foundry account. A freshly granted role takes a few minutes to
     propagate and returns 401 until it does.
     If your backend is a wizard-created "Azure AI Foundry" backend it
     authenticates itself, so delete that line in BOTH files. Getting this
     wrong shows up as 401, not 404.
  3. The rewrite-uri below is relative to the backend Runtime URL, and it
     ASSUMES that URL ends in /openai, exactly as
     wizard-foundry-policy-basic.xml requires. If yours is instead the bare
     account root, put the /openai back on the template:
     "/openai/deployments?api-version=2023-03-15-preview". Both files must
     make the SAME assumption about the backend, or one of them 404s.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY IT LISTS DEPLOYMENTS INSTEAD OF CALLING /openai/v1/models
  ===========================================================================
  The account root /openai/v1/models returns the base MODEL CATALOG, not your
  deployments: the ids do not match the names callers actually have to send,
  and the payload carries fields that trip strict client parsers. The data
  plane deployments list is the correct surface, and 2023-03-15-preview is
  the api-version that still serves it. The outbound section reshapes that
  response into the OpenAI /v1/models shape clients expect.
  ===========================================================================
-->
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <set-header name="api-key" exists-action="delete" />
    <set-header name="Authorization" exists-action="delete" />
    <set-backend-service backend-id="REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FOUNDRY-BACKEND-ID" />
    <!-- Delete this line if the backend already carries its own credentials. Must match the API policy. -->
    <authentication-managed-identity resource="REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FOUNDRY-MI-AUDIENCE" />
    <!-- Relative to the backend URL, which is assumed to end in /openai. Re-add /openai here if it does not. -->
    <rewrite-uri template="/deployments?api-version=2023-03-15-preview" copy-unmatched-params="false" />
  </inbound>
  <backend>
    <base />
  </backend>
  <outbound>
    <choose>
      <when condition="@(context.Response.StatusCode == 200)">
        <set-body><![CDATA[@{
          var outData = new JArray();
          try {
            var src = context.Response.Body.As<JObject>(preserveContent: true);
            var arr = src["data"] as JArray;
            if (arr != null) {
              foreach (var d in arr) {
                var id = (string)d["id"];
                var status = (string)d["status"];
                // A deployment still provisioning would be advertised but not yet usable.
                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(id) && (status == null || status == "succeeded")) {
                  outData.Add(new JObject(new JProperty("id", id), new JProperty("object", "model"), new JProperty("created", 0), new JProperty("owned_by", "azure")));
                }
              }
            }
          } catch (Exception) { }
          return new JObject(new JProperty("object", "list"), new JProperty("data", outData)).ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None);
        }]]></set-body>
        <set-header name="Content-Type" exists-action="override">
          <value>application/json</value>
        </set-header>
      </when>
    </choose>
  </outbound>
  <on-error>
    <base />
  </on-error>
</policies>
